// THE COAT - a short film for TERRA, built on the four costumes already on her card.
//
//   python3 studio/compile.py studio/movies/terra_field_coat.movie --timeline
//   python3 scripts/short.py studio/movies/terra_field_coat.json
//
// The writing, and the reason for every choice below, is in craft/THE_FILM.md.
// Five things to know before reading the file:
//
// 1. THE FOUR MOVEMENTS ARE THE FOUR COSTUMES, in the order her own card puts them in.
//    armour (issued) -> court (decided about) -> default (running) -> field (chosen).
//    The field coat is the only garment she ever picked herself and the film is named
//    after it. `costume:` is set once per chapter; the damage rung moves inside it.
//
// 2. `costume:` IS NOT WIRED THROUGH compile.py YET, and it is the one thing that must
//    be fixed before a single frame is rendered. compose.resolve() already takes a
//    `costume` key and already reads TERRA's `costumes` map - studio/compose.py:2366
//    and :2427 - and studio/_tools/turnaround.py already passes one. compile.py does
//    not: `costume` is absent from VARS and absent from the dict at compile.py:684, so
//    the five lines below parse, are stored, and are then read by nothing. Every beat
//    renders in the DEFAULT traveller costume until two lines are added. It is written
//    here in the resolver's own spelling so the fix turns the film on with no edit to
//    this file. See THE_FILM.md, "THE ONE THING THAT IS NOT WIRED".
//
// 3. EVERY SHOT LINE NAMES A MOVER AND AN ACTION, in the first comma-clause, in the
//    participle form compose.derive_motion() reads. 17 of 20 beats derive their motion
//    from the shot line and NOT ONE beat falls to an accidental hold. The other three
//    are named cards: the two spoken beats, which have no shot line to derive from and
//    so get a staged performance instead, and one shot that is held ON PURPOSE.
//
// 4. SHOT SIZES ARE PINNED close / medium close-up / medium. The only two wides in the
//    film have nobody in them. Her frame_verdict puts the honest cut-off at wide and
//    her face_quality_verdict puts a full-body face at about 90 pixels.
//
// 5. EVERY CLOSE INSERT GETS ITS OWN SCENE AND ITS OWN FREE-TEXT PLACE. A place CARD is
//    a location and an insert is a surface, and the card's scenery nouns beat the two
//    words at the end of the shot line that ask for a close-up - compose.py calls this
//    place_vs_shot. The first compile of this film raised it; these five scenes are the
//    fix.

MOVIE terra_field_coat
  title: THE COAT
  logline: A soldier who has only ever been dressed by other people buys a coat.
  canvas: 1920x1080
  fps: 24
  engine: anime
  style: cel_anime_90s
  checkpoint: animagine-xl-4.0.safetensors
  face_weight: 0.6
  seed_root: terra-coat-1
  clip_secs: 6
  tags: cinematic

// ===========================================================================
// I - ISSUED.  Imperial plate. Somebody else's hands doing up somebody else's
// armour on her. The film opens on the buckle, not on her face, and does not
// show what she is being dressed FOR until the third shot.
// ===========================================================================
CHAPTER i_issued
  look: cold
  place: castle_courtyard
  costume: armour
  camera: static
  pace: normal
  cue: unease

  SCENE dressed
    transition: fade_black
    characters: TERRA
    emotion: neutral
    wear: 0
    shot: insert | two hands pulling a breastplate strap tight across her ribs, red tabard beneath the steel, close-up
    shot: react @push | a steel gauntlet pushing the throat buckle closed under her jaw, medium close-up
    shot: establish | banners lifting on their poles above the courtyard wall, an empty hay cart below, no humans, wide shot

  // Two axes at once, new place and new time, so this boundary takes the 0.70s
  // dissolve rather than a cut.
  SCENE sent
    transition: dissolve
    place: snowfield
    characters: TERRA
    emotion: neutral
    wear: 2
    shot: master | walking out of frame to the left, unbroken snow to the horizon, medium shot

  // The aftermath insert. Cut, never dissolve, into the consequence of the shot
  // before it.
  SCENE the_gauntlet
    transition: cut
    place: deep wind-crusted snow filling the frame, no horizon visible
    shot: insert | a steel gauntlet dropping through the frame into deep snow, close-up, no humans

// ===========================================================================
// II - DECIDED.  Court dress. The room where it is decided what she is, in front
// of her, without her. Nobody else is ever in shot. We never see who decides,
// because she does not get to see it either.
// ===========================================================================
CHAPTER ii_decided
  look: golden
  place: castle_great_hall
  costume: court
  camera: static
  pace: normal
  cue: tense_strings

  SCENE the_hall
    transition: fade_black
    camera: pull
    shot: establish | an iron chandelier swinging above a long timber table, empty benches below, no humans, wide shot

  // A DELIBERATE HOLD, and one of only two in the film. @hold_frame is the library's
  // single status=ready stillness card. She is stood at the end of a table and nothing
  // happens to her, because it is happening about her in a room she is not in. The
  // score drops out under it.
  SCENE decided
    transition: cut
    characters: TERRA
    emotion: neutral
    silence: true
    wear: 1
    shot: hold_silent @hold_frame @8s | she stands at the far end of the long table with her hands at her sides, medium shot

  SCENE she_says_it
    transition: cut
    characters: TERRA
    emotion: neutral
    motion: hand_to_face_only
    mood: the empty length of the table running away behind her, both hands at her waist, medium close-up
    wear: 2
    TERRA: Nobody will say which half.

  SCENE the_glove
    transition: cut
    place: worn stone flagstones filling the frame, dry rushes across the grain, no room visible
    shot: insert | a white glove dropping through the frame onto the flagstones, close-up, no humans

  SCENE her_fist
    transition: cut
    characters: TERRA
    emotion: neutral
    wear: 2
    shot: react @push | her fist closing on the edge of the table, medium close-up

// ===========================================================================
// III - THE ROAD.  Traveller, the clothes she happened to have on. The act where
// the world moves her rather than the other way round: handheld throughout, and
// she leaves the frame instead of entering it. This is the only costume that
// lands at all five damage rungs with the danbooru name in the prompt, so it is
// the one the film is allowed to ruin.
// ===========================================================================
CHAPTER iii_the_road
  look: overcast
  place: moorland
  costume: default
  camera: handheld
  pace: normal
  cue: desolate

  SCENE the_road
    transition: dissolve
    characters: TERRA
    emotion: neutral
    wear: 2
    shot: master | walking out of frame to the right, the open moor behind her, medium shot

  // The sash that blows out of frame here is the bandage on her forearm in the next
  // shot. The damage ladder is being used as continuity, not as decoration.
  SCENE the_sash
    transition: cut
    place: wet heather and peat filling the frame, no horizon visible
    shot: insert | a torn red sash blowing across the frame, close-up, no humans

  SCENE the_ford
    transition: dissolve
    place: riverbank
    look: storm
    characters: TERRA
    emotion: focus
    wear: 3
    shot: build | stumbling forward through shallow water over stones, medium shot

  // A hard cut into the purse, because it is a reveal and a reveal is cut to. We
  // never see whose hand held it out. The money that was not hers is one insert
  // long and is never explained.
  SCENE the_purse
    transition: cut
    place: a wet flat stone at the water edge filling the frame, no bank visible
    look: storm
    shot: insert | a leather purse dropping into an open hand, close-up, no humans

  // The lowest rung of the ladder, and the first thing in the film she takes.
  SCENE what_it_cost
    transition: cut
    place: riverbank
    look: storm
    characters: TERRA
    emotion: neutral
    wear: 4
    shot: react | her fingers closing over a leather purse at her chest, medium close-up

// ===========================================================================
// IV - CHOSEN.  Field coat. The act opens on the object rather than on the
// place, and the turn is an arm going into a sleeve. Everything here is static
// except one push, and that push is the same size and the same move as the
// buckle in shot two - opposite hands.
// ===========================================================================
CHAPTER iv_chosen
  look: dawn
  place: market_street
  costume: field
  camera: static
  pace: slow
  cue: quiet_dawn

  SCENE the_rail
    transition: fade_black
    place: the side of a market stall filling the frame, a row of iron hooks along a rail, no street visible
    shot: insert | a heavy brown coat swinging on a hook above the cobbles, close-up, no humans

  // hand_reach is status=weak and its verdict says it lands only where the hand is
  // already large in frame. It is staged that way on purpose: the mood line puts the
  // sleeve at her hand and the shot at medium close-up, which is the staging the card
  // measured at 0.904 and 2.231. This is the first time in the film she asks for
  // anything.
  SCENE she_asks
    transition: cut
    characters: TERRA
    emotion: tender
    motion: hand_reach
    mood: a brown coat sleeve hanging at her hand, a stall counter beside her, medium close-up
    wear: 1
    TERRA: How much for the brown one.

  // THE TURN. Silence under it, and the film's third and last push.
  SCENE the_sleeve
    transition: cut
    characters: TERRA
    emotion: resolve
    silence: true
    wear: 1
    shot: react @push | her arm pushing through the sleeve of a brown coat, medium close-up

  // The first and only shot in the film where she moves toward the camera. Her own
  // motion_verdict measured walk_in at market_street holding her frontal and stable
  // for the full 8.04s, which makes this the one place in the whole library where
  // this shot is known to survive its own length. Static camera: she does the moving.
  SCENE she_walks
    transition: cut
    characters: TERRA
    emotion: determined
    wear: 1
    shot: master @8s | walking forward toward the camera between the stalls, medium shot

  // The same moor as act three, in the coat, at golden hour. The last thing that
  // moves in the film is the only thing she ever chose, and she is still under it.
  //
  // THE PLACE IS THE MOORLAND CARD'S OWN GROUND NOUNS WITH ITS SKY TAKEN OUT, and it
  // has to be. studio/places/moorland.json ends in 'grey overcast sky, distant rain',
  // place is assembled BEFORE look, and earlier wins - so `look: golden` on the card
  // renders grey and the whole point of the reprise is lost. Checked in the compiled
  // prompt, not assumed. compose.py strips 'scenery, no humans' out of a place that
  // has a person in it, and has no equivalent for a place that names its own weather.
  // Act three keeps the card, because there the grey sky is what we want.
  SCENE the_moor_again
    transition: dissolve
    place: open moorland of heather and rough tussock grass rolling away over low hills, a broken dry stone wall crossing it, gorse
    look: golden
    cue: hopeful_rising
    characters: TERRA
    emotion: resolve
    wear: 2
    shot: hold_silent @8s | a heavy brown coat blowing across her legs, the open moor behind her, medium shot
